Here the trigram {{ill|Zhen|de|Zhen|ja|震|qq=Zhen (Bagua)|qq=ja|qq=震|lt=Zhen (震)|qq=draft|qq=simple|qq=User:Immanuelle/Zhen|qq=}} is regarded as representing the emergence of yang, being assigned to the initial crescent of the month; subsequently, the moon was seen as evolving through the phases represented by {{ill|Dui|de|Dui|ja|兌|qq=Dui (Bagua)|qq=ja|qq=兌|qq=zh-yue|qq=兌卦|qq=ko|qq=태 (괘)|qq=fr|qq=Duì|qq=nl|qq=Meer (trigram)|qq=pt|qq=Duì (I Ching)|qq=zh-min-nan|qq=Tōe-kòa|lt=Dui (兌)|qq=Dui (Bagua)|qq=ja|qq=兌|qq=zh-yue|qq=兌卦|qq=ko|qq=태 (괘)|qq=fr|qq=Duì|qq=nl|qq=Meer (trigram)|qq=pt|qq=Duì (I Ching)|qq=zh-min-nan|qq=Tōe-kòa|lt=Dui (兌)|qq=|qq=draft|qq=simple|qq=User:Immanuelle/Dui|qq=User:Immanuelle/Dui (Bagua)|qq=}}, {{ill|Qian|de|Qian|ja|乾|qq=Qian (Bagua)|qq=ja|qq=乾|lt=Qian (乾)|qq=draft|qq=simple|qq=User:Immanuelle/Qian|qq=}}, {{ill|Xun|de|Xun|ja|巽|qq=Xun (Bagua)|qq=ja|qq=巽|lt=Xun (巽)|qq=draft|qq=simple|qq=User:Immanuelle/Xun|qq=}}, {{ill|Gen|de|Gen|ja|艮|qq=Gen (Bagua)|qq=ja|qq=艮|lt=Gen (艮)|qq=draft|qq=simple|qq=User:Immanuelle/Gen|qq=}}, and {{ill|Kun|de|Kun|ja|坤|qq=Kun (Bagua)|qq=ja|qq=坤|lt=Kun (坤)|qq=draft|qq=simple|qq=User:Immanuelle/Kun|qq=}}. In this context the bright full moon represented by {{ill|Qian|de|Qian|ja|乾|qq=Qian (Bagua)|qq=ja|qq=乾|lt=Qian (乾)|qq=draft|qq=simple|qq=User:Immanuelle/Qian|qq=}} was associated with Jia, while the dark phase represented by {{ill|Kun|de|Kun|ja|坤|qq=Kun (Bagua)|qq=ja|qq=坤|lt=Kun (坤)|qq=draft|qq=simple|qq=User:Immanuelle/Kun|qq=}} was associated with Yi; the sun and moon were thought to meet as Ren and Gui from the north, before further entering the central positions of Wu and Ji.

== Heavenly Stems and Earthly Branches ==
Subsequently, the {{ill|Twelve Earthly Branches|qq=Earthly Branches|lt=Twelve Earthly Branches|de|Zwölf Erdzweige|ja|十二支|qq=draft|qq=simple|qq=User:Immanuelle/Twelve Earthly Branches|qq=User:Immanuelle/Earthly Branches|qq=}} were also employed, and the stems and branches were assigned to each {{ill|Yao|de|Yao|ja|爻|qq=draft|qq=simple|qq=User:Immanuelle/Yao|qq=}} of the Eight Trigrams.

